There are two types of errors with type = `version_conflict_engine_exception`:

First, is when we use versioning (which in our case is based on `edit_version` field). Obviously, it is useless to retry this operation because it will always fail.

Second, however, occurs when you send two upsert operations in parallel (i.e in two different bulk requests) on a doc with the same id like this:
```
var firstOperation = new UpsertOperation(id: "1234", doc: "{'foo': 100}");
var secondOperation = new UpsertOpertaion(id: "1234", doc: "{'bar': 777});

// thread1
...
bulkRequest1.add(firstOperation);
bulkRequest1.send();
...

// thread2
...
bulkRequest2.add(secondOperation);
bulkRequest2.send();
...
```

Your goal is to have this doc in ES in the end of the day:
```
{
   "foo": 100,
   "bar": 777
}
```

but since those upserts literally execute in parallel in ES, they may conflict and one of the bulk request will return with error message saying something like `version_conflict_engine_exception: tried to execute operation with seqNo=10 while expected is seqNo=11` that is because `seqNo` is an internal sequence number which ES assignes to each doc to ensure optimistic locking (different one from versioning).

This operation is safe to retry because that is what we actually wanted: to do an upsert of two different fields at the same time. Now, this is not 100% safe in terms of order of operation generally, but in our code we never update the same fields from two different threads, we only use upsert to populate our DocWithResult which is:
```
{
   doc: { ... },
   docgen_result: { ... },
   doc_story: { ... }
}
```
all these three fields are updated by independent stream processors and de-facto immutable, which means it is 100% safe to retry. 

This is by the one of the reasons why I want to get rid of `DocWithResult` and have 3 independent documents instead: we won't need upserts and we can get rid of this clunky code which differentiate between two different version conflict types (but that needs proving).

